          "Substantial reduction in oil spill risk and severity": 85
        },
        "justification": "Repurposing existing ballast tanks for emergency containment is highly feasible and scalable. It provides a temporary buffer post-incident, significantly aiding recovery and reducing the ultimate volume spilled, without affecting normal transport operations.",
        "total": 505
      },
      {
        "trace_id": "scamper-E",
        "scores": {
          "Resolves the technical contradiction": 70,
          "Technical feasibility": 60,
          "Cost and scalability": 65,
          "Transport continuity and economics preserved": 95,
