        },
        "justification": "Focusing on immediate transfer capability rapidly removes the cargo source from the damaged vessel, dramatically limiting spill severity. It is technically feasible but requires major global standardization and infrastructure investment in salvage capability (cost/scalability score reflects this). It preserves transport continuity and offers excellent environmental protection.",
        "total": 510
      }
